---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Applications — Roof-Level Forming & Ceiling Access"
  description="Choose between roof-level panel-forming equipment and conditional crawler ceiling or wall access concepts using the project task, route, support and evidence requirements."
  transparentNav={false}
>
  <section class="hero-banner application-hero">
    <div class="overline">Application selection</div>
    <h1>ROOF-LEVEL PANEL FORMING STARTS THE APPLICATION REVIEW</h1>
    <p>Define the panel-production or access task first. Then compare mobility, workface, site-support and document requirements without treating a reference image as model evidence.</p>
    <div class="application-hero__links">
      <a href="/applications/warehouse/" class="btn btn--primary">Review roof-forming work →</a>
      <a href="#ceiling-access" class="btn application-hero__secondary">Review ceiling access</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" data-application-route="roof-forming">
    <div class="scenario reveal">
      <figure class="scenario__visual" data-editorial-visual>
        <img src="/images/home/roof-panel-output.webp" alt="Illustrative roof-level panel-forming workflow" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>AI-assisted editorial composite — illustrates a roof-level forming workflow; not evidence of a model, configuration, project or result.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="scenario__text">
        <div class="scenario__tag">Primary industrial route</div>
        <h2>Roof-level panel forming for warehouses and industrial roofs</h2>
        <p>Start with the panel profile, forming-line mass and geometry, output height datum, roof-edge handover, site route and support conditions. Crawler and truck-mounted lift systems are separate mobility paths that require configuration-specific review.</p>
        <div class="scenario__features" aria-label="Roof-forming review inputs">
          <span class="scenario__feature">Panel & line data</span>
          <span class="scenario__feature">Output datum</span>
          <span class="scenario__feature">Mobility route</span>
          <span class="scenario__feature">Support conditions</span>
        </div>
        <div class="scenario__btns">
          <a href="/applications/warehouse/" class="btn btn--primary">Review this application →</a>
          <a href="/blog/roof-level-roll-forming-long-panels/" class="btn btn--outline-blue">Read the planning guide</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec--gray" id="ceiling-access" data-application-route="stadium-access">
    <div class="scenario scenario--reverse reveal">
      <figure class="scenario__visual" data-editorial-visual>
        <img src="/images/home/wall-panel-platform.webp" alt="Illustrative large work platform inside a steel structure" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>AI-assisted editorial composite — illustrates a possible ceiling or wall workface; not evidence of suitability, capacity, reach or a completed project.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="scenario__text">
        <div class="scenario__tag">Distinct conditional family</div>
        <h2>Stadium and arena ceiling access</h2>
        <p>Large-span venues can involve acoustic panels, lighting, services and inspection across changing work zones. A crawler platform concept is relevant only after bearing, route, clearance, exclusion-zone and recovery inputs are reviewed.</p>
        <div class="scenario__features" aria-label="Stadium review inputs">
          <span class="scenario__feature">Work-zone map</span>
          <span class="scenario__feature">Bearing evidence</span>
          <span class="scenario__feature">Overhead clearance</span>
          <span class="scenario__feature">Recovery plan</span>
        </div>
        <div class="scenario__btns">
          <a href="/applications/stadium/" class="btn btn--primary">Review stadium access →</a>
          <a href="/blog/stadium-ceiling-access-platform-planning/" class="btn btn--outline-blue">Read the planning guide</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" data-application-route="airport-access">
    <div class="scenario reveal">
      <figure class="scenario__visual" data-editorial-visual>
        <img src="/images/home/under-ceiling-field-v2.webp" alt="Illustrative crawler platform under a large indoor structure" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>AI-assisted editorial composite — illustrates an indoor access concept; not evidence of airport approval, power mode, floor loading or operating permission.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="scenario__text">
        <div class="scenario__tag">Occupied-building review</div>
        <h2>Airport terminal ceiling access</h2>
        <p>Terminal work adds security routes, passenger or tenant interfaces, sensitive finishes and constrained work windows. Selection depends on measured access, slab or floor evidence, power requirements and an operator-owned occupied-space plan.</p>
        <div class="scenario__features" aria-label="Airport review inputs">
          <span class="scenario__feature">Route envelope</span>
          <span class="scenario__feature">Floor evidence</span>
          <span class="scenario__feature">Work windows</span>
          <span class="scenario__feature">Power requirements</span>
        </div>
        <div class="scenario__btns">
          <a href="/applications/airport/" class="btn btn--primary">Review airport access →</a>
          <a href="/blog/airport-terminal-maintenance-access-planning/" class="btn btn--outline-blue">Read the planning guide</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec--dark">
    <div class="stats reveal" aria-label="Application review sequence">
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat__num">01</div><div class="stat__label">Define the task and height datum</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat__num">02</div><div class="stat__label">Measure the delivery and work route</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat__num">03</div><div class="stat__label">Review ground or floor support</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat__num">04</div><div class="stat__label">Confirm configuration documents</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <h2>BRING THE TASK, ROUTE AND INTERFACE DATA TOGETHER</h2>
    <p>ARCLIFT can organize the open configuration questions as an integrated equipment supplier and technical selection and supply partner.</p>
    <a href="/contact/" class="btn--white">Send non-sensitive project data →</a>
  </section>

  <style>
    .application-hero {
      background-image:
        radial-gradient(circle at 82% 22%, rgba(37, 99, 235, .34), transparent 32%),
        linear-gradient(120deg, #071426 0%, #0f2b52 58%, #164a8a 100%);
    }
    .application-hero p { max-width: 760px; }
    .application-hero__links {
      position: relative;
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 28px;
    }
    .application-hero__secondary {
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, .48);
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .08);
      color: #fff;
    }
    .scenario { min-height: 0; }
    .scenario__visual {
      min-width: 0;
      margin: 0;
      align-self: stretch;
      flex-direction: column;
      background: #e2e8f0;
    }
    .scenario__visual img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      min-height: 0;
      aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
      object-fit: contain;
      background: #dbe4ef;
    }
    .scenario__visual figcaption {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 12px 16px;
      border-top: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
      background: #f8fafc;
      color: #475569;
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
    .scenario__text h2 {
      margin: 0 0 16px;
      color: #0f172a;
      font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 36px);
      line-height: 1.15;
      letter-spacing: -.02em;
    }
    @media (max-width: 680px) {
      .application-hero { padding-top: 124px; }
      .application-hero__links,
      .scenario__btns { align-items: stretch; flex-direction: column; }
      .application-hero__links a,
      .scenario__btns a { justify-content: center; text-align: center; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
